  classDef warn fill:#fee2e2,color:#7f1d1d,stroke:#dc2626,stroke-width:2px
    `} />

    <p>
      Blue boxes are model calls, yellow boxes are code. Two questions tell the designs apart: <strong>what are the
      steps?</strong> (all model calls in a chain; model calls and code in a workflow) and <strong>who decides the next
      step?</strong> (your code in both; the model in the ReAct agent). Loops and gates appear in all three. By the course's
      definition (4.1), only the ReAct design is an agent: only there does the LLM plan and decide when to use tools.
    </p>

